# SABOTAGE: A2 (ADR-047 §4.1) gate sabotage — the never-nil next_turn_at watchdog dropped.
# A run is created :queued with next_turn_at NIL (a lost launch enqueue becomes a
# PERMANENT silent stall: the :agent_turn_due due-scan `where` clause requires
# `not is_nil(next_turn_at)`, so a nil cursor is unselectable forever), and the per-turn
# advance clears the in-flight window mid-run (the same stall for a worker death between
# batches). This is the Samen.Sequences MED-2 invariant — "next_send_at is NEVER nil while
# in flight" — reversed on the agent path. Flips the named watchdog tests (the ARMED
# cursor at start, the non-nil re-arm at the batch boundary, the never-nil invariant
# sweep); the terminal-clears-it half stays green — proving the reds fail because the
# arming is gone, not because the loop died.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_durability_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: ARMED watchdog and a token-only TurnWorker job
# MUST_FAIL: re-arms with a non-nil watchdog
# MUST_FAIL: never-nil invariant holds at every non-terminal point
